D1 keeps its accounting_docs rows after the host is set back to off, so "the
host holds documents" is not proof that the host is newer. Take-back now:
- refuses without the handover marker unless --force is passed;
- reads the host revision the handover recorded (host_state_rev in the marker)
  and only copies the host documents when that revision moved; otherwise it
  just lifts the freeze;
- lifts the freeze without touching anything when the host never took
  categorization over;
- exits non-

The Executive Overview stopped syncing on page load in 4e9971b;
useExecutiveBootstrap() has no caller. EDD and Pirsch now sync from the
pulse bar's Sync button, so the SYNC.md tier table says that instead.

withoutSassHedges() removes the hedged lines from the cloud prompt, so the
strict hedges cut had nothing to replace there. It stays a local arm;
scoped no longer chains it, and the default arms drop it.

prs.body:
Adds `modules/claude/agents/Explore.md`, a read-only search subagent:
- tools `Read`, `Grep`, `Glob`; `Bash`, `Edit`, `Write` and `Agent` disallowed;
- `model: haiku`, `omitClaudeMd: true`, `maxTurns: 12`;
- answers with file paths and short excerpts, and stops instead of guessing or proposing changes.

`statusline.sh` now handles claude-local sessions as well as cloud ones:
- context window from the loaded Ollama model's `context_length`, then Claude's reported window, then 200k (1M by name);
- every model Ollama still holds, with size and minutes until unload; last-turn tok/s (wall clock, prefill included) and Ollama prefix-cache reuse;
- cost only for Claude model names, so local tags never get priced at the Sonnet fallback rate.
